course: dictionary
lesson: 7185
title: Perspective
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A perspective is a way of seeing something, a point of view. The same thing can look different from different places. «From my perspective, the match was unfair» tells you what one person thinks, and someone else may see it differently.
explain: Perspective also means a way of drawing in art, so that far things look smaller and parallel lines seem to meet at a vanishing point. Look at the clues around the word. If the sentence is about roads, railways or drawing, it means art.
explain: To keep things in perspective is to see how big or small a problem really is. «Looking up is a simple way to put a problem in perspective» means the problem still matters, but less. Ask yourself: is this as bad as it seems?
fact: Perspective means a point of view, or a way of seeing something.
fact: In art, perspective makes things look solid and far away, with far things drawn smaller.
fact: «Put it into perspective» means it is not as bad as it seems.
fact: In stories, «first-person perspective» means the story is told by «I».
fact: «Forced perspective» is a camera trick: something close to the camera looks huge and something far away looks tiny.
exercise: «From my perspective, the team played well.» What does perspective mean here? | *A point of view, or way of seeing things | A kind of camera | A drawing of a railway | A long, narrow path
exercise: Ruby draws a road that gets smaller and smaller into the distance. What is this way of drawing called? | Shadow | Outline | Colour | *Perspective
exercise: «Looking up is a simple way to put a problem in perspective.» What does put a problem in perspective mean? | Make the problem bigger | *See how big it really is | Forget the problem completely | Draw the problem on paper
test: A story told from a «first-person perspective» is told by whom? | A camera | The reader | *The narrator, using the word «I» | A narrator called «he»
test: «Forced perspective» is a camera trick. What makes something look huge? | Being in the shade | *Being close to the camera | Being far away from the camera | Being drawn with curved lines
exam: Which sentence uses perspective to mean seeing a problem as less bad? | «The forced perspective trick made the tower look tiny.» | «The vanishing point is in the middle of the page.» | «He drew the railway with straight lines.» | *«Looking at something huge can put a small problem in perspective.»
